Lane Warden Production Battle Slice
Build: P2-0.16.1
Design baseline: 1.7
Stable install scope: /lol-the-spire/lane-warden-prod-v0.10.4/
P2 Living Battlefield: both tactical lanes now follow distinct curving terrain paths instead of straight rails. Ground variation, creek, scrub, stone, camps, objective approaches, and route markers make the field readable as a place.
Commander routing: Old Gate Steps, Dry Creek Ford, and Ridge Cut provide three spatially distinct cross-lane routes. The route system selects the shortest viable cut-through and preserves mid-move retargeting and reversal.
Camera: pinch zoom is now a true two-axis field inspection. Roads, scenery, structures, formations, health bars, effects, and labels all scale together up to 225%, with anchored horizontal and vertical panning.
Movement feel: cohort simulation remains unchanged, while presentation positions use state-aware damping, reduced bob/lunge amplitudes, dust, curved-path alignment, and slower cross-lane traversal to add weight and remove visual skating.
Tactical models: P2-0.16.0 model-derived miniature formations, casualty counts, reinforcements, structures, tower attachments, and source/license pipeline remain intact.
Combat, reward packets, progression, run persistence, encounter tuning, Reclamation, Last Stand, and deployment capacity are unchanged.
P2-0.15.1 delivery protections remain: explicit shell build marker, mixed-shell repair, stale-shell rejection, and build.json-last deployment discipline.
